-- Q815: Security and Control Frameworks [medium/L1]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Defense in depth employs multiple overlapping layers of security controls so that if one layer fails, others continue providing protection. Under NIST SP 800-53 Section SC-3, this layered approach minimizes single points of failure across network, host, application, and data layers.
Wrong (A): A single perimeter firewall creates one point of failure that exposes the entire environment if breached, contradicting the layered defense approach.
Wrong (C): Relying exclusively on strong passwords represents a single-factor, single-layer approach that provides no protection if passwords are compromised.
