-- Q826: Threats, Attacks, and Vulnerabilities [hard/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): The pattern of 50,000 failed login attempts from 200 different IP addresses in 30 minutes is consistent with a distributed credential stuffing or brute force attack. Under NIST SP 800-63B Section 5.2.2, attackers use stolen credentials from other breaches across many IP addresses to evade rate-limiting controls.
Wrong (A): A single user forgetting their password would generate attempts from one IP address with far fewer failures, not 50,000 attempts across 200 distributed sources.
Wrong (C): Normal authentication traffic does not produce 50,000 failures in 30 minutes; legitimate traffic shows high success rates during business hours.
