-- Q831: Security Controls and Monitoring [easy/L1]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Role-based access control (RBAC) assigns permissions to roles that map to job functions, ensuring all users in the same role receive identical, auditable permissions. Under NIST SP 800-53 Section AC-2, this simplifies administration across large user populations through a single role assignment.
Wrong (A): Granting individual permissions based on personal requests describes discretionary access control, which creates inconsistency and significant administrative burden across many users.
Wrong (C): Giving all users the same access level violates least privilege and provides no differentiation based on job responsibilities or security requirements.
Wrong (D): Time-based access control restricts when users can log in but does not address the role-based permission assignment described in the scenario.$EXPL$
