  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): The principle of least privilege requires that users, processes, and systems receive only the minimum permissions necessary to perform their authorized functions. Under NIST SP 800-53 Section AC-6, restricting the DBA to only the databases in scope directly applies this principle.
Wrong (A): Granting administrative access for self-service troubleshooting violates least privilege by providing elevated permissions beyond what job duties require.
