-- Q848: Privacy Requirements and Data Protection [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): The purpose limitation principle under GDPR Article 5(1)(b) requires that personal data be collected for specified, explicit, and legitimate purposes and not further processed in a manner incompatible with those original purposes. Using order confirmation emails for unsolicited marketing constitutes incompatible further processing.
Wrong (A): Data minimization addresses collecting only the data necessary for the stated purpose, not restricting use to the original purpose for which data was collected.
